{"name":"Bourbon","hex":"#af6c3e","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Bourbon","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A European dynasty which reigns in Spain and formerly ruled the Kingdom of France.","A surname from French."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Bourbon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bourbon whiskey","blocks":[{"text":"Bourbon whiskey is a barrel-aged American whiskey made primarily from corn (maize). The name derives from the French House of Bourbon, although the precise source of inspiration is uncertain; contenders include Bourbon County, Kentucky, and Bourbon Street in New Orleans, both of which are named after the House of Bourbon. The name bourbon might not have been used until the 1850s, and the association with Bourbon County was not evident until the 1870s."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/DecaturBourbons.jpg/330px-DecaturBourbons.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bourbon_whiskey"},{"title":"Brasseries de Bourbon","blocks":[{"text":"The Brasseries de Bourbon is the only major producer of beer on Réunion Island, formerly known as Bourbon Island, a French overseas department in the Indian Ocean."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/59/Brasseries_de_Bourbon.jpeg/330px-Brasseries_de_Bourbon.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brasseries_de_Bourbon"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Bourbon-bottle_from_Gettysburg.jpeg/500px-Bourbon-bottle_from_Gettysburg.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Bourbon-bottle_from_Gettysburg.jpeg/500px-Bourbon-bottle_from_Gettysburg.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ninet